<section image-layout="blank" id="eM-e-e61AX"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ir0VD4FE1k" padding="0" colspan="38"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/-yzAQBppAjftaZBkeWD5b.png" saved-media-id="pgbc223exi9xvpk" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="sculptural-hair-editorial" alt="Full-height medium-format fashion beauty portrait of an adult Latino model with a soft shoulder-length shag, short crown layers visibly releasing loose movement while the longer perimeter remains intact, broken fringe opening lightly across the forehead, hair fully visible from crown to ends, warm directional studio light, uncluttered gallery-cream background, restrained oxblood wardrobe, realistic strands and subtle film grain, no hands, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="xRaOniD3B9" vertical-align="center" padding="56pt 46pt" colspan="22"><h1 font-size="40pt">MOVEMENT 02 /<br/>The Soft Shag</h1><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="lg">Short crown layers release movement while a longer perimeter preserves length. A broken fringe keeps the outline light, loose and wearable.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption"><span text-color="#5A4A45">AI concept imagery — not salon work.</span></p></grid-item></grid></section>